  KS-1557 verify trusts certification evidence only when it is a genuine act (secuura_app, MULTI_TENANCY_ENABLED=true)
    ✓ SETUP - the role in this run's title is the role the product really connects as, and the branch is the branch the title says (6 ms)
    ✓ control - a GENUINE lineage certification (parent = the owner's document, data.contentHash = the parent's hash) is presented by v1 and v2 with the REAL certification id and time (1338 ms)
    ✓ RED - the caller cannot choose the certification TIME, TYPE or ISSUER ID that verify presents (data.certifiedAt / certificationType / issuerId are ignored) (1305 ms)
    ✓ RED - A's OWN parent with ANOTHER organisation's hash does not make that hash certified (the parent's hash must equal the child's) (1906 ms)
    ✓ RED - a caller cannot CHOOSE the certification evidence: an overridden data.certificationId is DROPPED, and both verify paths present the SERVER's id and never the caller's (fail closed) (1266 ms)
    ✓ v2 by documentId (the derived row on its own, so its parent is NOT in the result set and is looked up): the genuine act is presented, the foreign-hash child is not (2173 ms)
    ✓ the FILE routes (v1 and v2 verify-file hash the uploaded bytes) apply the same rule: a genuine certification is presented, a foreign-hash child is not (1602 ms)
    ✓ a caller in ANOTHER tenant reads the registry path (crossTenantLookup in pool mode): the genuine act is presented, the forged shape is not; without a tenant manager nothing is found (2197 ms)
    hand-planted derived rows (superuser SQL): shapes a forged or damaged row can take
      ✓ RED - cites a certification id that resolves to NOTHING (929 ms)
      ✓ RED - cites ANOTHER actor's REAL certification (the id exists; the row's own external id does not carry it) (1575 ms)
      ✓ RED - cites the actor's OWN real certification, but the row's external id does not carry it (only the external-id binding rejects this) (1273 ms)
      ✓ RED - cites a LEGACY-CERTIFIED document: it carries certificationType but no holderId, so it is not a certification row (only the holderId check rejects this) (1579 ms)
      ✓ RED - cites the pkey of a plain DOCUMENT, which is not a certification (1261 ms)
      ✓ RED - the row is OWNED by someone else than the certification's issuer (the shape a sign-cert / sign-wallet row on another actor's document takes) (1279 ms)
      ✓ RED - has NO parent link (1261 ms)
      ✓ RED - cites a certification-shaped row that lives in ANOTHER tenant (the lookup is in the derived row's own tenant) (959 ms)
      ✓ control - a planted row that is structurally the same as a genuine one (real certification, matching suffix, parent with the same hash) IS counted, with the REAL id and time (949 ms)

